        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The completed rows (width, length, area) are $(9,31,279)$, $(16,24,384)$, $(22,18,396)$, $(35,5,175)$ and $(x,40-x,40x-x^2)$. Lengths are in metres; areas are in square metres.",
          "worked": "Let the width be $w$ metres and the length be $l$ metres.\n$$\\begin{align*}2w+2l&=80\\\\w+l&=40\\\\l&=40-w\\\\A&=w(40-w).\\end{align*}$$\nFor width $9$ m, the length is $40-9=31$ m and the area is $9\\times31=279\\text{ m}^2$. Similarly, the remaining numerical rows are $(16,24,384)$, $(22,18,396)$ and $(35,5,175)$. For width $x$ metres, the length is $40-x$ metres and the area is $x(40-x)=40x-x^2$ square metres.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the restrictions on the value of $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0<x<40$.",
          "worked": "Both dimensions must be positive: $x>0$ and $40-x>0$. Hence $0<x<40$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Graph the rectangle’s area versus $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A=40x-x^2$ for $0<x<40$: a downward-opening parabola with vertex $(20,400)$ and excluded boundary points $(0,0)$ and $(40,0)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=40x-x^2\\\\A&=400-(x-20)^2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe vertex is $(20,400)$ and the axis of symmetry is $x=20$. Plot the values from part (a) and draw the parabola over $0<x<40$. The boundary points $(0,0)$ and $(40,0)$ are excluded because the garden must have positive dimensions.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p30-q7-c-solution-graph",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"areaBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"area function curve\"}],\"reference\":\"source page 30 Question 7(c); teacher page 25 R7(c)\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.12cm,y=0.012cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{areaBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\draw[->,black,line width=0.5pt] (-4,0)--(47,0) node[right] {$x$ (m)};\n\\draw[->,black,line width=0.5pt] (0,-45)--(0,480) node[above] {$A$ ($\\mathrm{m}^2$)};\n\\draw[black,dashed,line width=0.4pt] (0,400)--(20,400)--(20,0);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (20,0)--(20,-8) (40,0)--(40,-8) (0,400)--(-0.8,400);\n\\node[below] at (20,-8) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$20$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};\n\\node[below] at (40,-8) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$40$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};\n\\node[left] at (-0.8,400) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$400$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};\n\\draw[areaBlue,line width=0.8pt,domain=0:40,samples=101] plot (\\x,{40*(\\x)-(\\x)^2});\n\\draw[areaBlue,fill=white,line width=0.8pt] (0,0) circle[radius=1.5pt] (40,0) circle[radius=1.5pt];\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
